WHEN TO USE GENERATORS
-----------------------
  USE when:
  - Data is too large to fit in memory
  - You only need one item at a time (training loops, streaming inference)
  - You want composable, chainable pipeline stages
  - You need to read from disk, network, or any sequential source

  AVOID when:
  - You need random access (index into position 500 arbitrarily)
  - You need to iterate multiple times cheaply without re-generating
  - The dataset is small enough that materialising it is fine and
    simpler code is worth more than memory savings

